e_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X$ be integrable and $h$ a function with $h(X)$ integrable. Which expression is guaranteed to equal $\\mathbb{E}[h(X)\\mid X]$ almost surely?","options":["$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)]$","$h(\\mathbb{E}[X])$","$h(X)$","$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)]\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{X>0\\}}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5a383d404c1f50260c0bc1fb","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X,Y,Z$ be arbitrary bounded random variables, with no further relationships assumed. Which proposed extraction is guaranteed by taking out what is known?","options":["$\\mathbb{E}[Y^2X\\mid Y]=Y^2\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[Y^2X\\mid X]=Y^2\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid X]$","$\\mathbb{E}[XY\\mid Z]=X\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid Z]$","$\\mathbb{E}[X^2Y\\mid Y]=X^2\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid Y]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3726e8882e5357a683c65cef","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X,Y$ be integrable random variables and $h$ a bounded function. Combining taking out what is known with Adam's law, which identity is guaranteed?","options":["$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)Y]=\\mathbb{E}[h(X)]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)Y]=h(\\mathbb{E}[X])\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)Y]=\\mathbb{E}[h(X)\\mid Y]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[h(X)Y]=\\mathbb{E}[h(X)\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"00030b9b4f9a68346310c68a","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X$ be a nonconstant, nonnegative integer-valued random variable with $\\mathbb{E}[X^2]<\\infty$ and $\\mathbb{P}(X\\ge2)>0$. Given $X$, let $Y\\mid X\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(X,p)$ for a fixed $0<p<1$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[XY\\mid X]$?","options":["$pX^2$","$pX$","$p\\mathbb{E}[X]X$","$X^2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"79f45426934c8cded2d9284c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X,Y$ be integrable random variables, with $X$ nonconstant and $\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]=2X+1$. Which random variable equals $\\mathbb{E}[X+Y\\mid X]$ almost surely?","options":["$2X+1$","$X+\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$3X+1$","$\\mathbb{E}[X]+2X+1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"eaae04e99cf55aad736c05e8","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X$ be a random variable and $Y$ integrable. Set $A=\\{X>0\\}$ and assume $0<\\mathbb{P}(A)<1$. Which expression is guaranteed to equal $\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbf{1}_AY\\mid X]$?","options":["$\\mathbb{P}(A)\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]$","$\\mathbf{1}_A\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid A]$","$\\mathbf{1}_A\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c918a3ca339e9077df6194f9","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X$ be bounded and $Y$ integrable. Set $W=X^2$ and suppose $\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid W]=3$. Which expression is guaranteed to equal $\\mathbb{E}[X^2Y\\mid W]$?","options":["$3\\mathbb{E}[X^2]$","$3W$","$3X$","$W\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"14c2f2853611869cb7d80640","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X\\sim\\operatorname{Unif}(0,1)$ and, conditionally on $X$, let $Y\\mid X\\sim\\operatorname{Bern}(X)$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[XY]$?","options":["$\\tfrac{1}{3}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{1}{12}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4cc914f29963890a119803f3","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X,Y$ be random variables with $Y$ and $XY$ integrable. Which additional condition is sufficient to justify replacing $\\mathbb{E}[XY\\mid X]$ by $X\\mathbb{E}[Y]$?","options":["$X$ and $Y$ are uncorrelated","$X$ is bounded","$Y$ is a function of $X$","$\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]$ is constant almost surely"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c660672d102a097b809e972d","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X$ be a real random variable and $Y$ integrable. To apply the stated taking-out proposition with $h(x)=x^2$, which additional integrability condition must be checked?","options":["$\\mathbb{E}[|X|]<\\infty$","$\\mathbb{E}[|X^2Y|]<\\infty$","$\\mathbb{E}[X^2]<\\infty$","$\\mathbb{E}[|XY|]<\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bee0a4073cde2d6ec6310a6a","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which expression equals $\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)$ when all moments involved are finite?","options":["$\\mathbb{E}[X\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]]-\\mathbb{E}[X]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[X]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]-\\mathbb{E}[X]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]]-\\mathbb{E}[Y]$","$\\operatorname{Var}(\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X])$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d763a3caad4d0c54b6e5c371","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X$ be exponential with rate $1$ and, conditionally on $X$, let $Y\\mid X\\sim\\operatorname{Pois}(X)$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X^2Y]$?","options":["$2$","$6$","$24$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"592791f6c9823056c78dff39","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X$ equal $1$ or $2$ with probability $\\tfrac{1}{2}$ each. Let $Y$ be integrable with $\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]=X^2$. What is $\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)$?","options":["$\\tfrac{3}{4}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$","$0$","$\\tfrac{9}{4}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e19430a4112fb5ce1646f0d0","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X,Y$ be square-integrable random variables with $\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]=X$. Which expression is guaranteed to equal $\\mathbb{E}[(Y-X)X\\mid X]$?","options":["$X^2$","$X\\mathbb{E}[Y]-X^2$","$X(Y-X)$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"02c2f7fba7424e76cf884f1f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $X,Z$ be bounded random variables and $Y$ integrable. To simplify $\\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[XY\\mid X,Z]\\mid Z]$, which expression is guaranteed by taking out what is known and retaining the correct conditioning information?","options":["$X\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid Z]$","$\\mathbb{E}[X\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X,Z]\\mid Z]$","$\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid Z]\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid Z]$","$\\mathbb{E}[X\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]\\mid Z]$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f11339a6a042f68f0ed88cd1","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y$ and $g(X)$ be square-integrable, and set $m(X)=\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]$. Write $R=Y-m(X)$ and $H=m(X)-g(X)$. In the expansion of $\\mathbb{E}[(Y-g(X))^2]$, which argument justifies $\\mathbb{E}[RH]=0$?","options":["Split $\\mathbb{E}[RH]$ into unconditional means because $R$ and $H$ are independent.","Set $\\mathbb{E}[RH]=0$ because the known factor $H$ has unconditional mean zero.","Condition on $X$ and take out $H$, since $\\mathbb{E}[R\\mid X]=0$.","Set $\\mathbb{E}[RH]=0$ because the conditional variance of $R$ is constant."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c389b5769708e406d6805fba","time_limit":45},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_taking_out_what_is_known_237a4515_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Given $X\\sim\\operatorname{Unif}(0,2)$, the variable $Y$ has $\\mathbb{E}[Y\\mid X]=X^2$. What is $\\mathbb{E}\\big[Y\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{X>1\\}}\\big]$?","options":["$\\tfrac{4}{3}$","$\\tfrac{1}{2}$","$\\tfrac{7}{3}$","$\\tfrac{7}{6}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"19c27ae3eed63ab6c8858590","time_limit":40}]}}